# Custom Utilities and Variants

## Overview
Extend Tailwind CSS v4 with `@utility` and `@custom-variant`.

## @utility

Create reusable utilities.

```css
@utility aspect-video {
  aspect-ratio: 16 / 9;
}

@utility prose {
  max-width: 65ch;
  line-height: 1.75;
  color: var(--color-text);
}
```

Accept parameters:
```css
@utility p- {
  padding: calc(var(--spacing) * <value>);
}
```

## @custom-variant

Define custom variants.

```css
@custom-variant hover {
  @media (hover: hover) {
    &:hover { @slot }
  }
}

@custom-variant dark {
  .dark & { @slot }
}
```

## Examples

```css
@custom-variant prefers-contrast {
  @media (prefers-contrast: more) {
    @slot
  }
}

@utility underline-offset-4 {
  text-underline-offset: 4px;
}
```

## Best Practices

- Keep utilities single responsibility
- Name utilities semantically
- Avoid duplicating core utilities
- Document custom variants usage
- Test variants in all states
- Use CSS variables for theming
